# Line endings are LF everywhere in this repository, on every platform.
#
# Two things break otherwise, both silently and both only after a clone,
# which is the worst time to find out.
#
# MAP.md is generated with LF and compared byte for byte by the
# pre-commit hook. Checked out as CRLF it never matches, so the gate
# blocks every commit while reporting a stale map that is in fact
# current. That is a check reporting a cause it has not tested.
#
# .githooks/pre-commit is a bash script. Checked out as CRLF it fails on
# the shebang, or throws "\r: command not found". The hook then does not
# run at all, and a hook that does not run looks exactly like a hook
# that passed.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.md   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf

.gitignore     text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.githooks/*    text eol=lf

# Binary, never converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
